[{"order":1,"type":"heading","text":"Utility Functions in jQuery"},{"order":2,"type":"paragraph","text":"jQuery provides a set of utility functions that are incredibly useful for performing common tasks. These functions are attached directly to the jQuery object ($.) and offer efficient ways to manipulate arrays, objects, and strings. This tutorial covers four essential jQuery utility functions: $.each, $.map, $.trim, and $.extend."},{"order":3,"type":"subheading","text":"$.each(): Iterating Over Arrays and Objects"},{"order":4,"type":"paragraph","text":"The $.each() function is used to iterate over elements in an array or properties in an object. It provides a simple and consistent way to loop through data structures."},{"order":5,"type":"code","text":"// Iterating over an array
var myArray = ['apple', 'banana', 'cherry'];
$.each(myArray, function(index, value) {
  console.log('Index: ' + index + ', Value: ' + value);
});

// Iterating over an object
var myObject = { name: 'John', age: 30, city: 'New York' };
$.each(myObject, function(key, value) {
  console.log('Key: ' + key + ', Value: ' + value);
});"},{"order":6,"type":"paragraph","text":"In the array example, the callback function receives the index and value of each element. In the object example, it receives the key and value of each property."},{"order":7,"type":"subheading","text":"$.map(): Transforming Arrays"},{"order":8,"type":"paragraph","text":"The $.map() function is used to transform the elements of an array into a new array. It applies a callback function to each element and returns a new array containing the results."},{"order":9,"type":"code","text":"var numbers = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5];
var squaredNumbers = $.map(numbers, function(number) {
  return number * number;
});

console.log(squaredNumbers); // Output: [1, 4, 9, 16, 25]"},{"order":10,"type":"paragraph","text":"In this example, $.map() squares each number in the 'numbers' array and returns a new array 'squaredNumbers' containing the squared values."},{"order":11,"type":"subheading","text":"$.trim(): Removing Whitespace"},{"order":12,"type":"paragraph","text":"The $.trim() function is used to remove leading and trailing whitespace from a string. This is particularly useful when dealing with user input or data from external sources."},{"order":13,"type":"code","text":"var str = '   Hello, World!   ';
var trimmedStr = $.trim(str);

console.log(trimmedStr); // Output: 'Hello, World!'"},{"order":14,"type":"paragraph","text":"The $.trim() function removes the leading and trailing spaces from the original string, resulting in a clean string without extra whitespace."},{"order":15,"type":"subheading","text":"$.extend(): Merging Objects"},{"order":16,"type":"paragraph","text":"The $.extend() function is used to merge the properties of one or more objects into a target object. It's commonly used to set default options or combine configuration settings."},{"order":17,"type":"code","text":"// Shallow copy
var defaults = { name: 'Guest', age: 0 };
var options = { name: 'John', city: 'New York' };

var settings = $.extend({}, defaults, options);

console.log(settings); // Output: { name: 'John', age: 0, city: 'New York' }

// Deep copy
var defaultsDeep = { address: { street: 'Main St', number: 123 } };
var optionsDeep = { address: { city: 'Los Angeles' } };

var settingsDeep = $.extend(true, {}, defaultsDeep, optionsDeep);

console.log(settingsDeep); // Output: { address: { street: 'Main St', number: 123, city: 'Los Angeles' } }"},{"order":18,"type":"paragraph","text":"In the shallow copy example, properties from 'options' overwrite properties in 'defaults'. The first argument '{}' creates a new object to avoid modifying the original 'defaults' object. The deep copy example ($.extend(true, ...)) recursively merges nested objects."},{"order":19,"type":"paragraph","text":"By setting the first argument to 'true', $.extend performs a deep copy, merging nested objects recursively. Without 'true', it performs a shallow copy, where nested objects are simply referenced, not copied."},{"order":20,"type":"paragraph","text":"These utility functions are essential tools for any jQuery developer, providing efficient and concise ways to handle common tasks related to data manipulation and object management."}]
